"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. The surgical findings included a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pathological stage pT3a with extraprostatic extension, but negative surgical margins and no invasion of the seminal vesicles were noted. The absence of lymph nodes removed and the lack of lymphovascular invasion are favorable findings. Preoperative PSA was 6.6.\n\nA significant uncertainty arises from the missing biopsy grade and ISUP report, which widens the uncertainty regarding the true tumor characteristics. Furthermore, the lack of nodal sampling means that the status is pNx, which does not equate to pN0, thus increasing uncertainty regarding regional disease control. The postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory are critical missing pieces of information that would substantially revise this prognosis. The current heuristic horizon suggests a follow-up period within a specific range. The fixed estimated horizon is 46.77 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 28.06–65.48 months; its coverage has not been validated."
